---
type: agent/instruction
description: Hand an existing linked worktree to a fresh agent session
usage: "guide://_worktree/use[/<worktree-name>]"
requires-handoff-context: true
requires-worktree-support: true
includes:
  - ../_partials/handoff-context-target
  - ../../_system/_handoff-context
elicitation:
  worktree-path:
    message: "Choose the linked worktree to hand over."
    schema:
      type: object
      properties:
        worktree_path:
          type: string
          source: worktree-inventory
      required: [worktree_path]
---
{{>handoff-context}}

{{#args.0.value}}
Using the current Git worktree inventory, read {{>handoff-context-target}}.
Locate `projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{args.0.value}}`; if it is absent,
acquire the shared lock and migrate applicable legacy context as instructed above.
The entry must then exist, and its recorded absolute `path` must appear in the
fresh Git worktree inventory. If either check fails, do not allocate a
replacement name or hand off a child; refresh or repair the handoff entry first.
Use its recorded resumable information as the child handoff.

Before assigning the child, create or initialise the target worktree's effective
configured workflow file with `worktree: {{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, preserving
its workflow state. Retain the existing handoff entry under
`projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.

Give the child the worktree name `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`, its absolute
recorded path, and the complete handoff entry. Do not forward this session
ID. The child must work from that path, create a fresh Guide interaction, bind
the shared project root and that worktree, then read its local workflow file
before workflow or handoff-context operations.
{{/args.0.value}}

{{^args.0.value}}
{{#elicit.worktree-path}}
The selected linked worktree is `{{kwargs.worktree_path}}`. Read its effective
configured workflow file before taking the shared handoff-context lock. If the
file has a valid non-`root` `worktree` label, retain that label and use or
repair its corresponding handoff entry. Otherwise, use Guide's allocated
label `{{kwargs.worktree_name}}`.

Acquire the shared handoff-context lock. Record or update the selected path at
`projects.{{project.name}}.worktrees.<label>`, including its required
`timestamp`, `path`, and the instructions for the child. Initialise the
selected worktree's effective configured workflow file with that same label,
preserving its workflow state, before assigning the child.

Give the child the final label, absolute selected path, and complete handoff
entry. Do not forward this session ID. The child must work from that path,
create a fresh Guide interaction, bind the shared project root and that
worktree, and read its local workflow file before workflow or handoff-context
operations.
{{/elicit.worktree-path}}
{{/args.0.value}}
